\f1\b \cf0 Below, you'll find some information to better understand this project.
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 1) AIMS OF THE PROJECT:
\f0\b0 \
\
First of all, it's important to clarify something as fundamental as it is banal: this collection is not about liturgical music! Far be it from me! This is absolutely not the context. These songs are not intended for use in church or during prayer.\
These are songs to be played and listened to in secular situations: at home, while working, listening to them on headphones, with a stereo, in the car, with family, with friends, etc. BUT NOT IN CHURCH! It is not liturgical music!\
\
I also want to offer a recommendation of etiquette, as a good father should:\
Since we are Catholic, and we have Our Lord Jesus Christ as our example, let us also try to be polite and set a good example for others, so don't disturb others while listening to music, keeping the volume appropriate in public places (unless you want to play it in a club, outdoors, or at a Catholic festival).\
I also advise you to be 
\f2\i "...wise as serpents and innocent as doves"
\f0\i0  (Matthew 10:16), especially when you listen to songs that contain very critical content towards certain cultures!\
\
I've always wondered: why is Christian music, and especially Catholic music, so rare, so lacking in inspiration and content, so timid, so tepid, with lyrics that are sometimes meaningless or lacking in true communicative power, and often even musically lacking, with banal melodies, banal lyrics, perhaps only useful for catechizing preschoolers, or truly bland, lacking in brilliance... Why?\
Actually, I know the reasons very well. But I won't write them down.\
As a great music enthusiast, I've been researching Christian bands and singers for years, and I've noticed that within the Protestant and especially Evangelical world, there are many groups that produce music that's also quite good. But this requires significant investment and solid production companies to promote them. Meanwhile, within the Catholic world, people have somewhat given up. Am I wrong?\
Apart from a few very rare cases, how many singers and musicians are there who are truly CATHOLIC and who sing CATHOLIC songs? Very few. A rarity! Try to think about them and list them.\
This situation has always saddened me deeply. And I've always thought it was a gap, a cultural void that needed to be filled. It's a missed opportunity for evangelization and apostolate, an untapped space. Some didn't believe in it and didn't invest in it.\
\
With this humble, timid, tiny project of mine, perhaps I have the opportunity to try to place at least some valuable content in that vast abyss.\
\
Initially, I was simply interested in producing enjoyable music for myself, and especially for my children, to provide them with a valid alternative to the contemporary musical degradation, which is crowded with anti-values \uc0\u8203 \u8203 and negative examples. I wanted to produce quality music so that my children could grow up listening to edifying, Catholic, traditional values, educating them about the Truth in general, and the Truths of our Catholic and Apostolic faith.\
\

\f1\b Indulging in a little good music is not a sin and cannot be denied, especially to young people! But why abandon them to the fate of listening to the vulgar and satanic trash played on the radio and TV, even accompanied by videos full of diabolical messages??!!\
I'm not having it!!! I want more for my children!!!\
\
With these songs, and their lyrics packed with useful information, my intent is to correct doctrinal errors, scientific errors, and in general cultural errors or misunderstandings that seriously damage the spiritual path and endanger the eternal salvation of souls.
\f0\b0 \
\
As I wrote above, I initially thought of producing songs just for myself and my family, but then I realized the results were satisfactory, so I tried sharing some songs on social media to see how my contacts responded.\
The reactions were good, so I decided to make these songs available to anyone who might be interested.\
\
I really want to clarify one fundamental thing:\
Many of the songs I write have fast tempos. Some have a techno base up to 150 bpm.\
The main genres are electronic, dance, rock, and pop. I made this choice deliberately, since there's already a lot of soft religious music.\

\f1\b It would be foolish to create alternatives to liturgical or classical music. Eternal masterpieces like Gregorian chants, or Schubert's Ave Maria, or Caccini's version... they certainly don't need alternatives!
\f0\b0 \
Do you agree?\
My songs are intended as alternatives to contemporary rock, pop, electro, and dance music. I hope I've been clear. I know that anyone who doesn't read this explanation will criticize me later, saying "these songs are too fast-paced to be religious music." But no one is forced to listen to my music! My main target audience is young people.\
If anyone doesn't understand this, they can listen to other music. Period.\
\

\f1\b In summary, the main goals and objectives I aim to achieve with these songs are the following:
\f0\b0 \
\
- Musical alternative to contemporary musical degradation\
\
- Evangelization and Apostolate\
\
- Spiritual combat\
\
- Fight against heresies\
\
- Catholic outreach\
\
- Scientific dissemination\
\
- Catechesis\
\
- Correction of falsehoods and erroneous beliefs\
\
I'm not interested in financial gain. I'm not interested in making money, since I'm a fortunate person. 
\f3\i\b "The Lord is my Shepherd, I shall lack nothing!"
\f0\i0\b0 \
My goal is only to help souls!\
Even fame isn't for me; I'm not interested! I prefer my songs to speak for themselves, without a face, without vanity! In total opposition to the spirit of the world, which instead transforms singers and musicians of dubious skill into vain IDOLS and "stars" intoxicated by success and money, worshipped by exalted crowds but musically illiterate and spiritually empty, at the service of vice and social engineering projects for mass control and with base goals including the depravity of youth!\
For this reason, I have adopted a pseudonym. If I derive any benefit from this work, it will not be in this life, but only in Heaven with God.\
I pray to the Lord that this tiny work of mine may ease my pain in Purgatory when I pay for my sins.\
I ask kind-hearted people to say a prayer for me; that is all I ask. Thank you! May the Lord bless you!\
\
\

\f1\b 2) THE PRODUCTION METHOD:
\f0\b0 \
\
I'm not a professional musician, but I studied music for several years and have a diploma in clarinet. I've always been a huge music lover, of all genres. And I have a vast music collection. In my actual profession, I work in video editing, video editing, and audio editing, so I've been working with music regularly for about 20 years. I'm also an experienced IT technician.\
\
The lyrics for these songs are written entirely by me in the traditional manner (without the use of any generative tools!).\
In some songs, I use quotes from sources of intellectual inspiration, such as papal encyclicals, official documents of the Holy Office, the Holy Bible, the Gospels, or other books, or prayers.\
\
The music, however, is generated using generative algorithms and audio editing software available today, which I cover financially. I pay for. You just have to listen to the result of my work.\
As I wrote in a song: 
\f2\i "We sow the seeds of Truth. We do it only for Charity. Some seeds will bear fruit, while others will change everything!"
\f0\i0 \
The plural is a must, since I'm not the only one who evangelizes or carries out apostolate, but I'm referring to the communion of the faithful of our beloved and suffering Holy Catholic Church.\
\
To produce the backing tracks, I use generative tools (AI) because producing complex songs like these, with the same quality, would take years and financial investments that I absolutely cannot afford. Furthermore, it wouldn't be possible alone; it would take more people.\
If you want to listen to this music for free, this is the only way.\
The alternative is to ignore me and continue listening to whatever is out there. No one is forcing you to listen to my songs.\
\
\

\f1\b Production Phases:
\f0\b0 \
1- Writing the topic\
2- Rewriting the text, adjusting it to meter and/or rhyme\
3- Uploading the text into AI software\
4- Voices: choice of voices, tone, character, intonation, style, mood\
5- Choice of musical styles, style combinations, and fusions\
6- Choice of musical instruments, specifications for musical solos\
7- Choice of BPM (beats per minute)\
8- Choice of digital effects and digital instruments\
9- Annotations and additional instructions\
10- Multiple generation processes, interspersed with corrections and edits\
In total, for each song, I generate around twenty versions on average before arriving at the final one I'm satisfied with.\
For some songs, I generate versions in different styles and languages. Each of these, to achieve the desired result, requires an average of around twenty versions.\
The algorithms still have many limitations, so the corrections are numerous!\
It's a lot of work. I want people to understand that these songs don't just come out of a magic hat. There's work behind them. It may never be as extensive and demanding as that of real musicians in the recording studio or studio, but it's still commitment, time, money, and skills put into the service of SOULS!\
\
Enjoy listening!\
}
